---
import Workbench from '../components/Workbench';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Field Relay — compare local CSV exports</title>
    <link
      rel="icon"
      href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/') + 'favicon.svg'}
      type="image/svg+xml"
    />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Compare two local CSV exports by mapped ID, inspect exact row evidence, and download a review report without uploading files."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <noscript>
      <style>
        astro-island {
          display: none !important;
        }
      </style>
      <main class="case-study">
        <p class="eyebrow">FIELD RELAY / STATIC REFERENCE</p>
        <h1>A browser-only CSV reconciliation desk.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          JavaScript is needed to compare two mapped CSV exports, inspect their exact rows, record
          local review decisions, and download the findings. The separate delivery lab is fictional.
          Nothing is uploaded or sent.
        </p>
        <p>
          Read how the comparison keeps source evidence and why the separate fictional delivery lab
          quarantines conflicts and prevents a repeat local delivery.
        </p>
        <p><a href="case-study/">Read the case study and workflow boundaries</a></p>
      </main>
    </noscript>
    <Workbench client:load />
  </body>
</html>
